WEBVTT

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:16.820
Libertá,

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.720
the only ones summoned to 
this emergency meeting

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:21.750
are those of the upper 
echelon of each serie.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:22.960
Why are you here?

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:26.790
Dante is out dealing with negotiations 
regarding coastal waters.

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:28.850
Negotiations?

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:31.260
I haven't heard anything 
in regards to that.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:33.630
Let's hurry.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:35.130
R-Right.

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:19.630
You're late!

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:23.870
What the hell are you so annoyed about?

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:25.210
Nothing in particular.

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:27.310
I just don't want to waste time.

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:32.810
Let us begin.

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:35.880
Pirates have landed on Regalo Island.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:37.420
Pirates?

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:40.820
They have kidnapped someone 
of importance to Regalo

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:42.490
and are currently on the run.

00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:43.890
Someone of importance?

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:45.260
Yes.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:47.810
Mondo's older brother, Moreno.

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:51.770
Papa's older brother?

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:54.920
Meaning Nova's dad?

00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:59.730
As you all know, 
he can't escape on his own.

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:01.020
That's right...

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:04.450
Nova's father has been in a coma 
due to a severe illness...

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:07.870
S-Sorry.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:10.870
I don't care. It's the truth.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:20.420
They're asleep because 
I put them to sleep.

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:25.050
What are they after?

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:26.180
Who knows?

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:28.770
I can't see a possible 
motive whatsoever.

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:32.490
We're going to wait 
for their next move,

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:33.980
so, for now, you'll all be on standby.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:37.450
How can you handle this so leisurely?

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:38.440
Shut up!

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:48.300
You are not to make a move 
until instructed to do so.

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:04.520
Why, you...

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:06.780
stupid stubborn chickpea!

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:08.260
Stop calling me a chickp—

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:10.330
How the hell can you be so calm

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:11.770
when your father's been kidnapped?!

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:13.600
Step up and say you're 
going to save him!

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:15.480
If it were me, I would go!

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:17.840
If I didn't, I'd regret it 
for the rest of my life!

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:24.150
Don't forget your place.

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:26.800
You dumbass!

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:28.450
My <i>place</i> has nothing to do with this!

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:30.760
Or are you going to say

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:33.920
that you don't care what 
happens to your father?!

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:35.870
Of course not!

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:40.180
Then why aren't you going?!

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:45.690
Let's go save him.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:55.100
You're right.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.590
If the three of us go, 
it should work out.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.020
The three of us?

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:03.990
You, Princess, and me, duh.

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:08.950
The three of us will 
be able to save him,

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:11.850
and make it back safely.

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:12.870
Exactly.

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:20.960
Follow me. We're going to the harbor.

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:24.840
See? You <i>were</i> worried.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:38.100
So you're certain that your dad 
is being held on that ship?

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:41.840
I had the Holy Grail's 
coast guard look into it.

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:44.280
Let's use that.

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:08.090
I'm not sensing anyone's 
presence at all.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:11.700
Let's split up and look for him.

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:12.310
No.

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:14.540
We don't know how many 
of them there are.

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:17.380
It'd be unwise to split up our 
numbers without knowing.

00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:33.820
Well, that's interesting.

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:39.600
By the way, how long is the hostage 
in the cellar going to be asleep?

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:42.580
I hear he's been asleep for years.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:45.340
For years? Why?

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:48.930
I heard Death's got his soul.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:13.260
P-Princess...

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:14.860
What?

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:23.670
What's with this guy?

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:38.060
Be on your guard, Princess.

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:40.520
You, too, Libertá.

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:00.630
Still so many of them?

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:01.460
Leave it to me!

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:10.570
Princess!

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:16.210
I-I'm fine.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:25.470
Nova,

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:27.010
leave these guys to us.

00:08:27.010 --> 00:08:28.600
Hurry and find your dad!

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:34.360
That's my line.

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:35.260
What?!

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:39.280
You actually think the two of 
you could handle this many?

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:41.900
What the hell?!

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:43.660
You're saying that you can?

00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:48.130
I have the power of Death.

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:53.560
Go!

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:54.470
Nova!

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:56.590
You're in the way.

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:02.020
Go!

00:09:02.510 --> 00:09:04.390
Fine! Come on, Princess!

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:12.390
La Tenebrore Addormentato!

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:23.290
Sleep!

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:33.510
This is...

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:36.080
Nova's Arcana power?

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:43.680
Nova!

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:46.840
If you're going to go, hurry back.

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:49.150
If I lose consciousness,

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:53.410
my power will wear off 
and they'll wake up.

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:56.280
They'll wake up?

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:59.720
The reason my parents are still asleep

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:03.120
is because I lost control of my powers.

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:08.140
Libertá!

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:10.220
Hurry!

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:12.800
Are you going to be okay if we 
leave you here by yourself?

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:15.760
Who do you think you're talking to?

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:20.460
Let's hurry.

00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:21.210
Right.

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:43.930
Princess.

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:46.210
I told you before

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:49.700
that I would live by my sword, right?

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:52.960
Why are you bringing that up now?

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:55.360
In truth,

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:58.720
I'm just making excuses.

00:10:58.720 --> 00:10:59.690
What?

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:02.720
Nova reminded me.

00:11:04.190 --> 00:11:05.850
If he hadn't used his Arcana powers,

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:08.810
there's no way we would have 
gotten out of that situation.

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:12.870
I guess there is a difference

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:15.800
between not wanting to use them and 
not being able to use them.

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:20.740
Libertá, did you already 
forget what you told me?

00:11:21.640 --> 00:11:23.370
What I told you?

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:26.530
Even if you can't now, 
you will be able to someday!

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:28.970
Right?

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:36.920
It's odd. When you say that, 
I actually feel like I will.

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:38.280
Really?

00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:41.380
I've also said this before, right?

00:11:42.650 --> 00:11:44.890
That you have powers, Princess.

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:50.740
You somehow make everything work out.

00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:25.260
Princess, is this the guy?

00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:27.510
Yes. I'm sure of it.

00:12:36.140 --> 00:12:37.320
Must stay conscious...

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:00.610
Father.

00:13:07.420 --> 00:13:08.460
Thank you.

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:18.460
So, you can make a face 
like that, too, I see.

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:21.480
What kind of face are 
you talking about?!

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:24.900
I'm sorry.

00:13:26.770 --> 00:13:29.840
There's no way a child 
wouldn't care about

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:31.530
what happens to their parent.

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:11.700
Are you...

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:19.240
Libertá!

00:14:20.690 --> 00:14:21.660
Leave it to my...

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:23.550
Power of Death!

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:25.420
You idiot!

00:14:26.910 --> 00:14:29.100
Like I'd let someone as worn out as you

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:31.670
use their Arcana powers!

00:14:31.670 --> 00:14:33.110
Just shut up and watch!

00:14:33.110 --> 00:14:34.090
But...

00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:35.470
Did you forget?

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:37.180
We came here

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:42.070
to save your dad and 
make it back safely!

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:56.870
You've got me to deal with, too.

00:14:57.880 --> 00:14:59.670
I have no intention of losing

00:15:01.160 --> 00:15:02.770
with Princess at my side.

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:27.820
Do you really think it's wise 
to look so confident?

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:30.630
Let's show him, Libertá!

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:31.220
Yeah!

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:39.290
You idiot!

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:43.500
S-Sorry!

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:46.690
Look out!

00:15:51.690 --> 00:15:53.380
<i>At this rate, we can't win.</i>

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:57.280
But we have the upper hand in numbers.

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:03.150
Princess, I'll hold him off.

00:16:04.030 --> 00:16:04.980
Use that opening.

00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:06.320
Right.

00:16:11.350 --> 00:16:14.030
<i>I can't throw these... like this.</i>

00:16:17.960 --> 00:16:19.120
Now, Princess!

00:16:24.260 --> 00:16:25.920
Take this!

00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:34.340
Libertá!

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:35.880
It's all thanks to you, Princess.

00:16:39.950 --> 00:16:40.720
No!

00:16:41.650 --> 00:16:42.390
Princess!

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:47.820
I can do it, too.

00:16:49.390 --> 00:16:51.780
Pensiero Realizzare.

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:56.160
Shatter!

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:11.680
That's right...

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:16.300
I did this back then...

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:21.220
Libertá!

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:32.900
Boss!

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:35.270
Thanks for your hard work, men.

00:17:36.260 --> 00:17:38.230
It's for the runt.

00:17:38.230 --> 00:17:40.700
Putting on this little 
act was no big deal.

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:44.430
This is as far as I can help you.

00:17:46.030 --> 00:17:49.700
You three need to realize 
exactly how weak you are

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:51.970
and try your best to grow.

00:17:51.970 --> 00:17:55.000
And become stronger in time

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:57.010
for the Arcana Duello.

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:09.600
Princess! You're not hurt, are you?

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:11.090
It'd be more awkward 
if she wasn't hurting,

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:12.850
sleeping in a place like this.

00:18:12.850 --> 00:18:15.150
Why do you always have 
to take that tone?

00:18:19.380 --> 00:18:21.610
The mansion's underground cellar?

00:18:27.310 --> 00:18:28.370
Jolly!

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:30.460
Is my father safe?

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:32.140
Where's the masked man?!

00:18:32.870 --> 00:18:34.980
We've secured Moreno.

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:42.100
I haven't seen a report 
regarding a masked man.

00:18:42.790 --> 00:18:43.560
What?

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:47.630
When you three and Moreno 
were found at the harbor,

00:18:47.630 --> 00:18:51.430
apparently there was no 
trace of the pirate ship.

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:56.400
I'd like to say it was a job well done,

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:58.840
but disobeying orders is 
still disobeying orders.

00:18:58.840 --> 00:19:01.360
Normally you'd get a more 
severe punishment.

00:19:02.170 --> 00:19:04.660
However, given your achievements,

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:08.170
I'll let you off with one night and 
two days in the underground cellar.

00:19:08.170 --> 00:19:09.960
You should be thanking me.

00:19:10.310 --> 00:19:11.370
Wha—

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:12.650
Agreed.

00:19:12.650 --> 00:19:13.170
What?!

00:19:13.470 --> 00:19:16.140
I must say that you 
three are very lucky.

00:19:16.140 --> 00:19:17.490
What do you mean?

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:20.050
I just thought the whole 
incident seemed like a test

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:23.640
for you to use your Arcana powers.

00:19:27.130 --> 00:19:30.210
Of course, that's just how 
it played out in the end.

00:19:34.490 --> 00:19:36.480
Now that I think about it,

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:37.950
I used my Arcana powers...

00:19:37.950 --> 00:19:39.520
You used your powers?

00:19:39.520 --> 00:19:40.330
He did.

00:19:41.340 --> 00:19:43.880
And it's because of both 
of your Arcana powers

00:19:44.600 --> 00:19:48.080
that we were able to save 
Uncle and return safely.

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:51.540
Wait a minute!

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:54.840
Why does Jolly know what 
happened on the ship?

00:21:33.320 --> 00:21:35.420
Now, choose the one that 
should be punished

00:21:35.420 --> 00:21:36.560
by naming their card.

00:21:36.860 --> 00:21:38.170
Il Matto.

00:21:38.170 --> 00:21:39.420
La Luna.

00:21:39.420 --> 00:21:40.860
Il Matto.

00:21:41.150 --> 00:21:44.800
Tonight's sinner is you, Il Matto.

00:21:44.800 --> 00:21:46.860
Why the hell is it just me?!

00:21:46.860 --> 00:21:52.340
It was your idea to go 
save La Morte's father,

00:21:52.340 --> 00:21:53.540
was it not?

00:21:56.420 --> 00:22:01.070
The nocturne of corruption, 
Notturno version quarto.

00:22:01.070 --> 00:22:04.030
It's something I just 
finished last night.

00:22:06.790 --> 00:22:09.070
I'm pretty sure you won't die.

00:22:09.070 --> 00:22:10.690
Suck it up and start drinking.

00:22:10.690 --> 00:22:13.320
It's time for your repentance.

00:22:13.320 --> 00:22:14.590
All right.

00:22:21.570 --> 00:22:24.580
Your true repentance starts now.

00:22:24.580 --> 00:22:29.660
Il Matto, tell us about 
your time in the cellar.

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:30.490
Yes.

00:22:31.100 --> 00:22:33.910
The three of us, two men and one woman,

00:22:33.910 --> 00:22:36.290
were trapped in the cellar,

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:39.840
a situation that fueled our 
carnal desires like no other.

00:22:40.020 --> 00:22:42.340
Why are you talking like that?

00:22:42.340 --> 00:22:44.480
Princess must have been tired as

00:22:44.480 --> 00:22:47.160
she entrusted her soft, 
sweet-smelling

00:22:47.160 --> 00:22:49.440
body to the stone bed,

00:22:49.440 --> 00:22:51.740
and breathed softly in her sleep.

00:22:52.260 --> 00:22:55.500
Not knowing what was 
about to happen to her,

00:22:56.430 --> 00:22:59.670
her face totally relaxed in sleep,

00:22:59.670 --> 00:23:04.150
and her snow white thigh peeking out 
from the darkness of her clothes...

00:23:02.300 --> 00:23:04.150
What in the world was that 
drug you gave him?!

00:23:04.450 --> 00:23:06.560
A cocktail that allows

00:23:06.560 --> 00:23:08.320
one to answer with the carnal desires

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:11.600
they were feeling at the time 
of the question asked.

00:23:12.080 --> 00:23:13.380
As young as we are,

00:23:13.380 --> 00:23:16.120
it was more than enough to arouse us...

00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:18.410
Knock it off!

00:23:20.310 --> 00:23:23.760
You've rendered the sinner unconscious.

00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:26.740
I hope you're ready for 
your punishment, as well.

00:23:26.740 --> 00:23:29.190
S-Stop it!

00:23:31.330 --> 00:23:33.820
Next time's story is about 
going to Luca's secret base?

00:23:33.820 --> 00:23:34.960
Is that delicious?

00:23:34.960 --> 00:23:36.600
More importantly, 
can I get more lasagna?

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:37.810
If the lasagna is delicious 
and the sky is blue,

00:23:37.810 --> 00:23:39.130
I have no complaints.

00:23:39.130 --> 00:23:40.520
Well, see you again next week!
